{"id":2412,"path":"/listening/b1/stonehenge-b1-listening-test/","parentId":1142,"order":860,"section":"listening","level":"b1","depth":3,"title":"Stonehenge – B1 English Listening Test","seo":{"title":"Stonehenge – B1 English Listening Test - Test-English","description":"Listening comprehension test for intermediate students (CEFR B1). Watch a video about Stonehenge and choose the correct answers.","image":"/media/uploads/CEFR-B1-Listening_Stonehenge.jpg"},"modified":"2025-06-05T14:22:39","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>B1 English Listening Test</h3> <h5>Watch a video about Stonehenge. For questions 1 to 7, choose the correct answer.</h5> <p></p> <div class=\"videoWrapper\"> <div data-youtube=\"L2iFafYw9Yc\"></div> </div> <h6>For more videos like this, go to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL59GcrPDHI8KRjnxslMF13wbOQ8Uyb5Oh\">Loescher Editore video</a></h6> <div class=\"list-separator-dots\"><span>Questions</span></div> <div data-quiz=\"309\"></div>"],"explanation":null,"quizzes":[{"id":309,"questions":[{"id":2671,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Why was Stonehenge built here? </div>","choices":[{"id":4533,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Because it's a strategic point.</span>"},{"id":4534,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>We don't know.</span>"},{"id":4535,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Because there are rivers near the place.</span>"}]},{"id":2672,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How many people visit Stonehenge?</div>","choices":[{"id":4536,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Six thousand every day of the year.</span>"},{"id":4537,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>One million every summer.</span>"},{"id":4538,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Six thousand every summer day.</span>"}]},{"id":2673,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Stonehenge was built ...</div>","choices":[{"id":4539,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>5,000 years ago</span>"},{"id":4540,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>2,500 BC</span>"},{"id":4541,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>2,500 years ago</span>"}]},{"id":2674,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>What do we know about the people who built it?</div>","choices":[{"id":4542,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>The place where they lived.</span>"},{"id":4543,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Nothing.</span>"},{"id":4544,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>We know a little about their rituals. </span>"}]},{"id":2675,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>What do we know about the stones?</div>","choices":[{"id":4545,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>They all come from Wales.</span>"},{"id":4546,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>The small rocks come from far away. </span>"},{"id":4547,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>They all come from 25-30 Km away.</span>"}]},{"id":2676,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How did they carry the stones?</div>","choices":[{"id":4548,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Probably using animals.</span>"},{"id":4549,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Probably a lot of men were needed. </span>"},{"id":8410,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Using advanced technology for that time. </span>"}]},{"id":2677,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Which of these theories does he mention about why it was build?</div>","choices":[{"id":4550,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Astronomical calendar.</span>"},{"id":4551,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Ritual sacrifices.</span>"},{"id":4552,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Religious. </span>"}]}]}]}